KNOWNBUG libstdcxx
main.cpp
--cpp17 --object-bits 12 --unwind 8 --no-unwinding-assertions
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ vector<int> deduced from a braced list: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
[over.match.class.deduct]/2, [over.match.list]/1: for a braced list, the
guide from vector's initializer-list constructor, vector(initializer_list<
value_type>, const allocator_type & = allocator_type()), is tried first,
with value_type the class's typedef of T: `std::vector v{1, 2, 3}' is
vector<int>.  CBMC deduced vector<int, int> (CONVERSION ERROR): it tried
the guides with the elements as the arguments only, and libstdc++'s guides
were compiled out, as CBMC undefined __cpp_deduction_guides.
